Transitive closure
==================

Part of CACHE_FRAMEWORK: kernels kept as a separate set for cache studies
(cache locking and cache-miss analysis).

What it tests
-------------

Cache behaviour of graph code with irregular, data-dependent accesses.

What it does
------------

One partition, P1, with one periodic process.

Computes the transitive closure of a graph (DIS Stressmark "transitive
closure"). Period and time capacity: 1 s.

Expected output
---------------

"Transitive closure" every period; "ASSERT Failed" would report a wrong result.

Origin
------

Ported from DIS Stressmarks
(https://www.ics.uci.edu/~amrm/hdu/DIS_Stressmark/DIS_stressmark.html).

Build and run
-------------

From the top-level directory (builds every benchmark; QEMU needs only the one):

    make benchmarks                     # x86_64
    make BSP=arm64-qemu benchmarks      # arm64

    qemu-system-x86_64 -vga none -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/transitive/build/x86_64-qemu/pok.elf
    qemu-system-aarch64 -M virt -cpu cortex-a53 -m 1G -nographic \
        -kernel benchmark/CACHE_FRAMEWORK/transitive/build/arm64-qemu/pok.elf

To build only this benchmark, run "scons bsp=x86_64-qemu" (or bsp=arm64-qemu)
in this directory with POK_PATH set. The benchmark runs forever; quit QEMU with
Ctrl-A X.
